WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.667
Accuracy.

2
00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:06.633
It is the first metric everyone learns, and on rare events, the most misleading.

3
00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:11.133
Accuracy is the fraction of predictions that were correct.

4
00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:14.167
Add the true positives, the positives we caught.

5
00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:17.433
Plus the true negatives, the negatives we rejected.

6
00:00:17.733 --> 00:00:20.233
And divide by the total number of predictions.

7
00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:23.025
Imagine a thousand rows.

8
00:00:23.025 --> 00:00:27.800
Nine hundred ninety are negative, and ten are habitable zone candidates.

9
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.930
A lazy model always says no.

10
00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:33.067
It gets all nine hundred ninety negatives right.

11
00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:35.767
But it misses every one of the ten candidates.

12
00:00:36.967 --> 00:00:37.919
And the score?

13
00:00:37.919 --> 00:00:41.795
Ninety nine percent accuracy, with zero candidates found.

14
00:00:41.795 --> 00:00:43.767
Stellar accuracy, zero value.

15
00:00:44.967 --> 00:00:46.533
Here it is in scikit-learn.

16
00:00:46.833 --> 00:00:50.500
A dummy classifier that always predicts the most frequent class.

17
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.467
Its accuracy is zero point nine nine, which looks amazing.

18
00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:55.982
Its recall is zero.

19
00:00:55.982 --> 00:00:57.133
It caught nothing.

20
00:00:58.333 --> 00:00:59.667
So when can you trust it?

21
00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:03.767
Only when classes are roughly balanced and all errors cost the same.

22
00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:07.322
And always compare against the majority class baseline.

23
00:01:07.322 --> 00:01:10.933
If it scores point nine nine too, your model learned nothing.

24
00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.500
Here is a real story.

25
00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:18.300
Habitable zone candidates are about one percent of the exoplanet table.

26
00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.833
A demo proudly reports ninety nine percent accuracy.

27
00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:25.692
Then you show the dummy baseline also scores ninety nine.

28
00:01:25.692 --> 00:01:29.000
From then on, accuracy is banned from the slide deck.

29
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.000
Let's recap.

30
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.867
Accuracy is correct predictions over total.

31
00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:36.267
On rare classes, it is deceptive.

32
00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:38.567
Always check the majority baseline.

33
00:01:38.867 --> 00:01:40.200
Next up: precision.
